00:20:45.000 --> 00:21:16.000
We did a study in which people watched a movie, and for some of the people in our experiment, we didn't let them watch how the movie ended. We didn't let them see what happened to the main character. However, I asked you, which of these two movies would you rather see? A hundred percent of the hands go up and said, like to see the end of the movie, please. But what we discovered was, people who didn't see the end of the movie liked it more, thought about it for longer, were still engaged in it and still enjoying it, even hours or days later.
他们没有看到主角最后发生了什么，所以他们一直在想：天哪，我想知道他是否上了大学，或者他是否成为了足球运动员。思考并享受这些是一件多么有趣的事情。所以重点是，一点点不确定性可以让你非常快乐，但我们似乎从不想要它。如果明天你的门口出现了鲜花，没有纸条，只写着“秘密崇拜者”，我敢打赌你会付我很多钱去找出那个秘密崇拜者是谁，但我保证无论他是谁，

